# ── Whitelist approach: ignore EVERYTHING, then re-include only source code ──
# This guarantees no stray large files (.venv, models, caches, db dumps)
# ever leak into the build context, no matter what sits in the folder.
*

# Re-include application source
!main.py
!__init__.py
!requirements.txt
!analysis/
!config/
!core/
!integrations/
!knowledge/
!llm_backend/
!triage/
!rag/

# Re-exclude junk / data that lives inside the whitelisted source dirs
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/*.pyd
rag/chroma_db_metadata/
